From: mi5-droidspaces-kernel <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] module: warn but accept CRC mismatches for stock vendor modules

The stock ROM ships binary vendor modules (qca_cld_wlan.ko for WiFi,
exfat.ko, br_netfilter.ko, the wil6210 stack, ...) built against Xiaomi's
kernel with the original defconfig.

Droidspaces needs the IPC namespace, which on 3.18 requires SYSVIPC and/or
POSIX_MQUEUE.  Both add sysvsem, sysvshm and mq_bytes to struct task_struct, and
genksyms hashes the whole reachable type graph, so task_struct -> mutex ->
device, module, seq_file, ... renumbers thousands of exports that have nothing
to do with IPC, including functions the vendor modules import (seq_read,
pci_set_master, ...).

Those exports still use the same calling convention and every struct a driver
instantiates or dereferences (sk_buff, net_device, pci_dev, device, file,
cfg80211_*, ...) keeps its stock layout; only the textual type graph above the
changed struct differs.  Without this patch insmod rejects the modules and the
phone loses WiFi, exFAT and packet filtering, so keep loading and print a
rate-limited warning instead.

If a vendor module ever misbehaves, these warnings are the first thing to check.

--- a/kernel/module.c
+++ b/kernel/module.c
@@ -1172,9 +1172,23 @@
 	return 0;
 
 bad_version:
-	printk("%s: disagrees about version of symbol %s\n",
-	       mod->name, symname);
-	return 0;
+	/*
+	 * Enabling the IPC namespace (SYSVIPC/POSIX_MQUEUE) adds sysvsem,
+	 * sysvshm and mq_bytes to struct task_struct.  genksyms hashes the
+	 * whole reachable type graph, so task_struct -> mutex -> device,
+	 * module, seq_file, ... renumbers thousands of unrelated exports.
+	 * Those exports keep the same calling convention and every struct a
+	 * driver touches keeps its stock layout, so a mismatch here is not a
+	 * real ABI break for the stock vendor modules on this device.
+	 *
+	 * Refusing to load would leave the phone without WiFi
+	 * (qca_cld_wlan.ko), exFAT (exfat.ko) and packet filtering
+	 * (br_netfilter.ko), so warn once per symbol and keep going.
+	 */
+	if (printk_ratelimit())
+		pr_warn("%s: disagrees about version of symbol %s (ignored)\n",
+		       mod->name, symname);
+	return 1;
 }
 
 static inline int check_modstruct_version(Elf_Shdr *sechdrs,
